cff-version: 1.2.0
title: idtrackerai-detectron2
message: >-
  This repository is a modified version of idtracker.ai. The tracking
  method is the work of the de Polavieja Lab. If you use this software,
  please cite their paper (given under preferred-citation) first. Cite
  this repository in addition only if the Detectron2 segmentation path
  itself is relevant to what you are reporting.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bellio
    given-names: Martina
repository-code: https://github.com/mbel-tech/idtrackerai-detectron2
url: https://github.com/mbel-tech/idtrackerai-detectron2
abstract: >-
  A fork of idtracker.ai that accepts animal outlines from an external
  instance-segmentation model, such as a fine-tuned Detectron2 Mask
  R-CNN, in place of its own intensity thresholding. Identity tracking
  is unchanged: crossing detection, fragmentation, identification and
  gap closing run exactly as in upstream idtracker.ai.
keywords:
  - animal-tracking
  - instance-segmentation
  - detectron2
  - mask-rcnn
  - idtracker.ai
  - behavioural-analysis
  - fish-tracking
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
date-released: '2026-09-20'

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    New idtracker.ai: rethinking multi-animal tracking as a
    representation learning problem to increase accuracy and reduce
    tracking times
  authors:
